WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.840
Thanks for the meal!

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.660
Did I eat too much for breakfast?

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.530
Fall makes you hungry.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.900
And you can't stop eating Ruriko-san's cooking!

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.150
Huh?

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.380
How cute!

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.860
Kuri's imitating the tsukimi 
dumplings we made!

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.120
Nice, Kuri...

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.070
That looks fun!

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.110
Let me play, Kuri...

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:25.990
Let's make a castle now.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.310
I want to join in!

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.280
Me, too!

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.080
We have to go to school, though.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.240
What you guys doing—

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.960
Strike!

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.040
What are you doing, you old hag?

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.790
Who are you calling an "old hag"?!

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.860
Kuri!

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.770
Now, you've done it...

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.190
You'll pay for that.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.190
What a sight.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.170
Chirp! Chirp! Chirp!

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.420
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.900
Another quiet day, chirp.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.040
Another peaceful day, chirp.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.450
Nothing out of the ordinary, chirp!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:39.430
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.880
<b>Seventeenth Haunting 
The Road to Hell Is Paved With Good Intentions</b>

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.220
Almost being late is rare for you, Inaba.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.980
I got... involved in a mud 
fight this morning...

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.310
Damn, I'm late?!

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.730
Okay, time's up!

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.600
Chiaki-sensei?

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.030
Come on, run...

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.670
We're saved!

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.770
Thanks, Chiaki-sensei.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.660
If you want to be grateful, wake up earlier.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.030
It will make our lives easier.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.150
Stop it!

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.460
All right, I'll read it.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.330
This is one of my favorite Bible verses.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.270
Do any of you know it?

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.720
You don't have to understand the meaning.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.340
The important thing is that 
you hear the English.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.760
"No temptation has overtaken you, 
but such has come into man.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.360
And God is faithful.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.490
He will not allow you to be tempted 
beyond what you're able.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.450
But with the temptation, he will 
provide a way of escape, also."

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.520
<i>Chiaki and Aoki are kind 
of opposite types, huh?</i>

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.160
<i>Chiaki's popular with rebellious boys,</i>

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.240
<i>and Aoki's popular with studious girls.</i>

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.380
<i>Being popular with people of your 
own sex requires a special charm.</i>

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.540
<i>Well, either way, it's good to be popular.</i>

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.520
Yamamoto?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.960
How did that test go?

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.180
Awful.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.200
I guess I did okay.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.350
Seriously?

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.980
She's...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.010
Hey, Yama—

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:21.950
Inaba-kun,

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.350
could you come with me?

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.620
Sure.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.420
I heard your parents passed away when 
you were in middle school, right?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.620
That must have been hard.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.170
Y-Yeah...

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.710
You really are working hard.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.880
I'm sure your parents are happy!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.640
R-Right...

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.120
<i>What is this?</i>

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.050
<i>You aren't a part of my life, 
so why are you saying this?</i>

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.990
I'm not your homeroom teacher,

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.810
but I am your English teacher.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.970
If anything comes up, please talk to me.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.860
I'll always listen to you.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.760
S-Sure...

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.070
Thank you.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.150
You aren't the only one who's suffering.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:19.570
Many people suffer and work hard, anyway.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.760
You aren't alone!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.490
Let's do our best together!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.400
I'm back.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.520
<i>I don't really think of myself as suffering.</i>

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.860
<i>I don't know why, but I feel mad!</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.190
Master?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.950
Inaba!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.900
Listen to me!

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.140
What's up?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.860
I was talking with Chiaki-chan in the hall.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.070
And Aoki-sensei came...

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.660
It's true, Chiaki-chan!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.970
Inaba's so funny!

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.250
It's fun to play with him—

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.550
Tashiro-san?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.660
Y-Yes?

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.480
You shouldn't do that.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:10.500
Call him "Chiaki-sensei" like 
you're supposed to.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.850
O-Okay...

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.480
And, Chiaki-sensei?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.700
Please stop touching the 
female students without reason.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.940
N-No, Aoki-sensei! Chiaki-chan—

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.680
I mean, Chiaki-sensei didn't do it. 
I wrapped my arm around his!

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.290
It isn't his fault!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.860
This isn't your fault, Tashiro-san.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.780
Chiaki-sensei is in the wrong 
for not refusing to let you.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.910
As a teacher, if he'd cared about you,

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.710
he should have rejected the gesture 
more firmly. Isn't that right?

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.870
Thanks for the speech.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.550
B-But...

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.710
It's all right.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.100
You didn't know anything.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.880
It's we teachers who have to teach you.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:57.290
And let's all try to call male students 
"-san," instead of "-kun."

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.800
But make sure you definitely 
use one or the other.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.030
That's how it works in the adult world.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:03.960
Once you're out there, you'll have trouble.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.990
So make it a habit now.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.900
Okay.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.320
What a great teacher!

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.680
She really cares about us!

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.360
Sakura, are you serious?

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.810
I was really mad!

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:21.660
Why?

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.530
Wh-Why?

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.030
I'm not really sure, but...

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:30.300
Well, I'm sure she's just thinking about us.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:36.710
But that doesn't necessarily mean 
she really understands you.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:38.510
What do you mean?

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.660
In other words, you call me "Inaba."

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:46.220
But you use "-san" for older students 
in the club or your boss at work.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:49.200
Of course. Even I do that.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.030
She probably thought that you didn't.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.520
I see. That's why I...

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.740
She's concerned about you.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.510
But Aoki only sees a part of you.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.760
A part of us?

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.710
She only sees a part, but she 
acts like she sees it all.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.060
That's why you got mad.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.950
<i>And me, too.</i>

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.890
<i>Without my parents, it's lonely and hard.</i>

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.670
<i>That's true.</i>

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.960
<i>But that doesn't mean I feel like my life is ruined.</i>

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:26.090
<i>But without talking with me, 
without seeing anything,</i>

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:31.190
<i>Aoki decided how things were for 
me, based on her own values.</i>

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.420
<i>That's what made me so mad.</i>

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.340
It's none of her business!

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:37.780
That's great!

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:41.690
If Aoki talks to me again, 
that's what I'll say!

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.630
That it's none of her business.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:46.130
That's great! Say it with a 
big smile on your face!

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:47.620
Very elegantly!

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.650
How lively!

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.390
A-Aoki-sensei...

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.750
I was going to give this to Inaba-kun.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.970
For me?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.970
<b></b>

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.910
What is it? An English dictionary?

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.110
It's the one I use.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:05.410
I thought it would help Inaba-kun 
with his English studies.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.570
No, I...

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:07.690
It's fine.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:12.160
You probably don't have the money for 
it, unlike an ordinary school book.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.740
<b></b>

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.730
So just take it.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:17.110
Everyone, don't think I'm playing favorites.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:20.660
You all understand that Inaba-kun 
is special, don't you?

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.070
None of you are handicapped, 
so let's support him together!

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.550
Even Inaba-kun can do his best because 
everyone is here for him, right?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.160
Bye. Good luck with your studies.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.500
Sensei!

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:40.010
I'm not special, and I don't 
feel handicapped!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.640
That's right! Hang in there!

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.280
I-Inaba?

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.070
<b></b>

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.980
Screw you!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:05.490
Handicapped? Let's all support him?!

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.900
That's none of her business!

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:08.540
Damn it!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.110
Calm down, master!

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.990
Your aura is fluctuating badly!

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.000
Shut up!

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:16.010
Damn it!

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.090
You got something!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.680
What's this?

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.020
<b>From Hase</b>

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.020
Hase?

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:27.620
<i>"Hey, Inaba.</i>

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.970
<i>Doing well?</i>

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:32.660
<i>I'm writing this in Germany, 
at Lichtenstein Castle.</i>

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.340
<i>When you touch the world's winds,</i>

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:38.230
<i>you understand how small you really are.</i>

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:41.170
<i>You should travel the world, too.</i>

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:45.160
<i>I'll be back soon with presents, 
so look forward to it.</i>

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.380
<i>From Hase."</i>

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.780
Tch. You sure have it easy.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.830
You have finally calmed down?

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.620
Now, then... What is this wonderful scent?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.470
Oh, you're back.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.540
Today, we're having grilled fall salmon
with vegetables and salmon roe bowls!

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.800
It looks great!

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:25.870
At school, huh?

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.870
It's good to be young!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:32.650
Just listening to you makes this old 
salary man feel young again.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:36.210
Sato-san, why not be a student next?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:37.210
That's great!

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.700
I've never been a high school student.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.360
Want to come to my school?

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:45.300
We have lots of weird teachers
and new club members.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.970
<b>Barley
Shochu</b>

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.980
You seem quite tired, Yushi-kun.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.390
That's part of being young.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.800
Like an unripe fruit.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.770
And speaking of unripe fruit!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.550
Aoki-sensei!

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:03.000
She's covered herself in this silver armor 
that says, "I am absolute justice."

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.600
She's like the Maid of Orleans!

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.370
I bet she's kind of a pain!

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.610
Basically, she doesn't know 
how to express herself.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:16.670
She's so serious, she can't learn any 
other ways of seeing things.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.440
Someone from my department 
who had that problem quit.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.430
He was a nice guy,

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.450
and he'd care too much about new people.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:29.190
He'd take away jobs that the 
new guy had to learn,

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.100
without letting him do anything or speak.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:34.380
In the end, the new guy 
couldn't get any work,

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.740
and he wasn't able to grow...

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:40.230
Even if the boss tried to blame the new guy,

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.320
he'd come out and try to cover for him,

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.920
"He's still new, so he can't do that."

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:49.050
From the start, he decided that the 
new guy couldn't do anything.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.570
Being nice and caring isn't a good thing.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:56.890
What's good are the results 
that it can bring about.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.630
Sometimes, being harsh or doing 
nothing, can be kindness, right?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.140
That's it...

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.460
That's the difference between 
Aoki and Ryu-san.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.320
What's wrong, Yushi-kun?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:13.710
Fool once said that Aoki's aura 
was similar to Ryu-san's.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.810
Aoki-sensei and Ryu-san?

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.430
Indeed!

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:21.180
Their auras are both unperturbed 
by various feelings.

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.530
Perhaps you could call it strong belief!

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.730
But they're different! I know it!

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:28.650
When I first acquired the <i>Petit</i>,

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:31.500
Ryu-san said he'd help me all I needed.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.070
But he didn't do anything.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.130
When I suffered with my training,

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.940
he didn't give me any advice or help.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.020
But he was with me.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.040
He believed in me and watched over me.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:44.500
That was his kindness.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.510
But Aoki's kindness is the opposite.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.720
The worst part is that she doesn't realize 
that she's forcing her good intentions

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.850
on other people.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:56.320
Scary.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:57.550
Which means...

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:59.830
A toast to the maiden!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.730
You guys look like you're having fun.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.340
By the way, did you know, Yushi-kun?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.820
The road to hell is paved 
with good intentions.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.410
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:14.410
That does it for role assignments, right?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.440
So let's keep going until 
the day of the social!

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:18.930
I'm the star?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:21.590
I'll cave to the pressure before I 
even worry about the English!

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.240
Don't worry, Mamiya.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.400
Nobody expects acting ability from you.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.720
Well, you should, a little!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:40.520
<b></b>

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.360
You don't have a speaking part?

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.780
You ran, huh?

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:36.380
No! I have work, so I had them excuse me!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.510
I wanted to hear your terrible acting!

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:42.810
Okay, enough talk—

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.900
Yamamoto...

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.000
What?

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.280
Did she bring her resignation letter?

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.320
Hey, Yamamoto-san!

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:10.180
If you're at the club,

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.350
act like a club member.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:17.350
And how do I "act like a club member"?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.420
Listen...

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:23.020
We're all getting ready for what we're going
to do for the social with the Foreigners Club!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.000
Is that mandatory?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.940
I don't want to do it.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.930
Then, why did you come here?

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.320
If you want to read a book, 
go to the library.

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.610
Yamamoto, calm down, and let's talk—

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:48.640
Yama—

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:49.530
Yamamoto-san,

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.810
if you don't want to help 
prepare, that's fine.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:56.470
Just don't come to the club
until the social is over.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:00.090
Having one person reading and 
not participating is disruptive!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.710
Way to go, club president...

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.940
What's wrong?

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.830
That girl was crying.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.200
Aoki!

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.120
Um, this is...

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.780
Bullying is wrong.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.050
<b>Huh?!</b>

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.720
Lots of people surrounding 
a girl and making her cry.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:36.170
You're in high school, now. 
Shouldn't you be better than this?

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.310
It's so sad...

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.230
<i>Ow...</i>

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.780
No... Listen, Sensei.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:46.360
Let's be friends.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:50.340
If you bully someone, they aren't 
the only one who gets hurt.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.230
You get hurt, too!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.410
She's going in circles.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.530
I know.

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.530
What class is she in?

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:03.610
Why not go and talk to her 
homeroom teacher?

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:05.490
I'll help you!

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:08.270
We're fine, Sensei! No need to worry!

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.830
We'll handle it ourselves.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.920
I'm sure we'll make up...

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:15.750
I see.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.170
Nice work!

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:20.440
Good... I'm happy you understand!

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.910
What the hell was that?!

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.770
Does she have no idea what she's saying?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:39.960
The road to hell is paved 
with good intentions.

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:45.140
The road to hell is paved 
with good intentions...

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.790
That's scary, Isshiki-san!

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.330
What's scary?

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.420
Chiaki? What are you doing here?!

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.210
Ow!

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:02.800
Chiaki-sensei is on break.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:07.440
Aoki-sensei said that, huh?

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:13.030
Well, with people like that, 
you have to adapt to them.

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.700
Like your club president did.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.730
That's frustrating.

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:19.610
Is there no way we can talk it out?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.330
There is...

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.880
But you speak different languages,

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:29.820
so it takes an incredible amount 
of time and effort.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.060
Chiaki-sensei!

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:33.180
<i>Again?</i>

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:35.580
There, you are.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.210
We're having our teacher's meeting soon—

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.010
Oh?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.420
Inaba-kun?

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:46.920
I'm very sorry. I was talking with 
him, and I lost track of time.

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:48.200
Oh, Inaba-kun.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:51.850
Did you need to talk? You could 
have talked to me!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.810
N-No, it's nothing!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.740
Really?

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:57.270
Holding it in isn't good.

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:00.330
Aoki-sensei, you don't need to worry so much.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.150
He'll be fine.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.870
No, Inaba-kun has no parents,

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.920
and lives at his apartment alone.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.080
There's no end of worrying to be done.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.700
<i>I'm not alone!</i>

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:12.240
<i>If anything, there are too many people!</i>

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:18.100
And boys his age have many worries 
and frustrations, I know.

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:22.300
They make things out to be worse 
than they are or get too excited.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.360
<i>She's just deciding things again!</i>

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.440
Listen, Aoki-sensei...

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.340
When someone will do something stupid,

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:31.100
their daily life becomes a mess, first.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.390
Look at him.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.990
His shirt collar is clean.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:40.310
He's washing his shirts, wearing fresh 
ones, and keeping himself clean.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:42.950
His ears are clean, too. 
No piercings, either.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.490
And he hasn't dyed his hair.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:48.710
He's well-muscled, and his skin is smooth,

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.760
so he's eating and sleeping properly.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:52.990
Someone who's doing all these basics

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:55.420
doesn't need any help.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.120
<i>Th-That's...</i>

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.170
<i>That's what it was?</i>

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:10.550
Even so, he is still alone, isn't he?

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.660
Isn't he lonely when he doesn't 
feel well or isn't at school?

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:20.030
That doesn't mean you can 
hang out downtown, though.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.020
Just come and talk to me!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.360
<i>Again?</i>

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:32.320
Th-Thank you... I'll do that.

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:34.680
That makes me happy, Inaba-kun!

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:35.790
It's a promise!

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:39.950
Hurry along to the teacher's 
meeting, Chiaki-sensei.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.020
And...

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.330
You should stop smoking.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.660
That's none of your business.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.270
She doesn't speak a different language.

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:03.160
She just doesn't listen to me!

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.880
I told her I'm fine!

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.690
Arguing is a waste of time.

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:10.490
The more you say, the more she'll 
think, "I knew you were lonely."

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:11.690
But...

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:17.010
Well, I'm lucky that Class 2-C has nothing 
but good students like you.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:20.880
I can leave you alone, without worry.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.590
Chiaki...

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:25.930
It's "Chiaki-sensei."

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:30.470
<i>Someone's watching over you.</i>

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.880
<i>Someone believes in you.</i>

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.560
<i>Doesn't that make you happy?</i>

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.400
You know how guys always 
say, "Kids these days..."

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:17.000
When you say that, it means you're old.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.340
Really?

00:23:18.340 --> 00:23:20.320
But you say that sometimes, right?

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:23.830
When did I say that? Don't be stupid.

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:27.210
Jeez, kids these days are so...

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:31.340
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.430
Words From Deep Within Your Body.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.720
<b>Eighteenth Haunting 
Words From Deep Within Your Body</b>

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:36.190
What is true communication?
